-7be0c2e60925"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genome-wide association analyses identify 95 risk loci and provide insights into the neurobiology of post-traumatic stress disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.61-741800","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this introduction to the Special Section ‘Laboratory Times', the editors argue that a focused body of scholarship at the intersection of time and the laboratory has yet to materialize. To contextualize the papers that comprise the Special Section, we survey the role of the lab within time studies, as well as the place of temporality within Science and Technology Studies (STS). We show how time is made to structure and shape scientific practice and how scientists work with and create time to suit the frames and needs of experimentation. While one might expect to find as many forms of scientific time as there are branches of science, the specific temporalities of bench science have been largely overlooked by scholars. We introduce the arguments of the papers in this Special Section - observing their shared interest in the ways that time is materialized, negotiated and produced in laboratory settings. We conclude by imagining a future in which a research trajectory focused on ‘Laboratory TImes’ brings scholars in time studies and STS further into conversation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hussey, Kristin D.","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S02-083.33-751865"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Editorial","Laboratory studies","Review","STS","Temporality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction laboratory times","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103756782/Hussey_and_Douglas-Jones_2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-083.33-751865","identifier":[{"id":"85191238830","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7d5d6e30-f469-4bcf-877a-464430147211","ku-5f46869b-00f8-4ca0-b6d4-fc2d1c03e948"],"keyword":["STS","editorial","laboratory studies","review","temporality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2F14A319C9089EEB20C19D6EF592F823"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103756782/Hussey_and_Douglas-Jones_2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Medical Museion","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Metabolic Science in Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristin D.","key":"husseypau","last":"Hussey","locid":"78bd4901-720b-44c7-8020-2248cef8f3c9","name":"Hussey, Kristin D.","orcid":"0000-0002-4831-141X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0961463x241246397","issn":["0961463X","14617463"],"issn_org":["0961463X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Time & Society","pages":"237-250","status":"p","title":"Time & Society","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191238830"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7d5d6e30-f469-4bcf-877a-464430147211","ku-5f46869b-00f8-4ca0-b6d4-fc2d1c03e948"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction: Laboratory times","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.33-751865","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In 2019, the National Health Commission of China announced a nation-wide plan to incorporate blood donation into the country’s emerging informational infrastructure: the social credit system (SCS). Through analysis of comments from Weibo, one of China’s largest social media sites, alongside news articles and official government announcements from the time, we follow the figure of the basket, which we regard as vernacular critique. By analysing the formation of trust indicators, contestations over their commensurability, and the prospect of converting between moral deeds and financial advantage, we aim to augment understandings of the ways that quantification practices are, and become, moral projects.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jiang, Qiuyu","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S02-092.08-793372"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood","China","Data","Donation","Indicators","Weibo","basket","social credit"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"credit is a basket on the inclusion of blood donation in china s social credit system on the inclusion of blood donation in china s social credit system","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/cja.2024.420105","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.08-793372","identifier":[{"id":"85199417662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9fdb9a3b-2809-4a83-8c82-7d78c3227574","itu-d92aba46-2a9b-4790-952d-5239bf5f6bab"],"keyword":["China","Weibo","basket","blood","data","donation","indicators","social credit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A334632023847FC59A8098BB55ED4F37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/cja.2024.420105","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/432505927/_Credit_Is_a_Basket_On_the_Inclusion_of_Blood_Donation_in_China_s_Social_Credit_System.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Global Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiuyu","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","locid":"01816dda-4fa3-4b5a-b715-63f9158f9d96","name":"Jiang, Qiuyu","orcid":"0000-0002-6888-897X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3167/cja.2024.420105","issn":["03057674","20477716"],"issn_org":["03057674"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Cambridge Journal of Anthropology","pages":"61-81","publisher":"Berghahn Journals","status":"p","title":"The Cambridge Journal of Anthropology","title_org":"Cambridge Journal of Anthropology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199417662"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9fdb9a3b-2809-4a83-8c82-7d78c3227574","itu-d92aba46-2a9b-4790-952d-5239bf5f6bab"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘Credit Is a Basket’: On the Inclusion of Blood Donation in China’s Social Credit System : On the Inclusion of Blood Donation in China’s Social Credit System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.08-793372","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It is becoming increasingly difficult to address environmental questions without considering how they overlap and intersect with digital concerns. We observe and make our understandings of environments through, for example, digital devices, spreadsheet accounting and carbon calculations. Conversely, we make the digital through the appropriation of environmental forms; crafting metals and plastics into sleek handheld devices, while powering our data use through vast quantities of energy consumption. We have brought epochal shifts into being through rhetoric, disciplines, and geological measures. Yet the ‘we’ of these statements is an unevenly distributed set of actors, whose politics is pressing. While it is evident that the anthropocene is constituted through colonial histories, what this collection foregrounds is how deeply interwoven it is with the tools, devices, and computational logics that are part of such histories. In this special issue, we bring together four anthropology and Science and Technology (STS) scholars, each of whom offers a different empirical instance of approaching digital anthropocenes. Through various modes of sensing, governing, intervening, and speculating, each article reveals a particular colonial legacy that provokes an alternate form of politics (proto, limit, civic, and pre-figurative). What is revealed in each case, we claim, is the legacy of a colonial infrastructure that whilst saturated in forms of technological inequality and injustice also affords a counter political re-imagining through digital mediations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Andersen, Astrid","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S02-097.00-822397"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Maguire, James"],"keyword":["Anthropocene","Coloniality","Digital","Double Vision","Folds"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction approaching digital anthropocene s a double vision","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/introduction_nc6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.00-822397","ids":["aau-96f1f975-39d7-4f00-9937-c0fa5123841d","itu-5ef2369e-f96e-4ba3-8541-8b852b409fe9"],"keyword":["Anthropocene","coloniality","digital","double vision","folds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-32D01DF4D22E8AEE8825E4EFFD3A0803"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/journal/issue-6/introduction/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/introduction_nc6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humani