{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic returned the politics of ‘access’ to the forefront of anthropological discussion. This article offers a multimodal, autoethnographic account of ‘access’ across axes, foregrounding the biomedical, digital, bureaucratic and citizenship contingencies of arriving in China, a process which was for two of the authors, a process also of returning ‘home’. We employ the metaphor of the ‘blind box’, colloquially and commercially meaning a box containing mysterious toys, to unfold questions of power and uncertainty over one’s fate during pandemic travel. The article’s co-created comics, read alongside written narratives, convey affective environments, and aid our analysis of the changed and charged conditions of access. We therefore frame access through shifts in technological affordances, the affects they produce, and the risks and responsibilities that fieldworkers carry. We argue that in these stories, access becomes an experience to be lived through, saturated with the contingencies of technology as researchers find themselves subject to the fluid landscape of policy, shifting perceptions of ‘home’ and newly resonant parallels with earlier eras of ethnographic research in China.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tao, Han","Zhao, Hailing","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-822479"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Tao, Han"],"keyword":["Access","China","Covid 19","Digitalization","Ethnography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opening the blind box a multimodal account of access to the restricted field china during covid 000000000019","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26686/ce.v5i1.7698","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-822479","ids":["aau-dbf3dae5-5914-4456-8313-8484bb45142a","itu-994cecba-593d-468d-bf3b-cd7eaa52f5e3"],"keyword":["COVID-19","China","access","digitalization","ethnography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E21F63C87C895B0D93F0A280612D5546"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26686/ce.v5i1.7698","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495680/1._TaoZhaoDouglas_FINAL.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://ojs.victoria.ac.nz/ce/article/view/7698/7968","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Global Politics & Diversity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Han","key":"taopau","last":"Tao","name":"Tao, Han","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hailing","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"c50555a1-169c-4dbc-b749-ae69fe9385f1","name":"Zhao, Hailing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.26686/ce.v5i1.7698","issn":["25379879"],"issue":"1","journal":"Commoning Ethnography","pages":"7-37","publisher":"Victoria University of Wellington Stout Research Centre","status":"p","title":"Commoning Ethnography","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dbf3dae5-5914-4456-8313-8484bb45142a","itu-994cecba-593d-468d-bf3b-cd7eaa52f5e3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Opening the Blind Box : A multimodal account of access to the restricted field China during COVID-19","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-822479","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Immunometabolism considers the relationship between metabolism and immunity. Typically, researchers focus on either the metabolic pathways within immune cells that affect their function or the impact of immune cells on systemic metabolism. A more holistic approach that considers both these viewpoints is needed. On September 5–8, 2022, experts in the field of immunometabolism met for the Keystone symposium “Immunometabolism at the Crossroads of Obesity and Cancer” to present recent research across the field of immunometabolism, with the setting of obesity and cancer as an ideal example of the complex interplay between metabolism, immunity, and cancer. Speakers highlighted new insights on the metabolic links between tumor cells and immune cells, with a focus on leveraging unique metabolic vulnerabilities of different cell types in the tumor microenvironment as therapeutic targets and demonstrated the effects of diet, the microbiome, and obesity on immune system function and cancer pathogenesis and therapy. Finally, speakers presented new technologies to interrogate the immune system and uncover novel metabolic pathways important for immunity.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Cable, Jennifer","Rathmell, Jeffrey C.","Pearce, Erika L.","Ho, Ping Chih","Haigis, Marcia C.","Mamedov, Murad R.","Wu, Meng Ju","Kaech, Susan M.","Lynch, Lydia","Febbraio, Mark A.","Bapat, Sagar P.","Hong, Hanna S.","Zou, Weiping","Belkaid, Yasmine","Sullivan, Zuri A.","Keller, Andrea","Wculek, Stefanie K.","Green, Douglas R.","Postic, Catherine","Amit, Ido","Benitah, Salvador Aznar","Jones, Russell G.","Reina-Campos, Miguel","Torres, Santiago Valle","Beyaz, Semir","Brennan, Donal","O'Neill, Luke A.J.","Perry, Rachel J.","Brenner, Dirk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-680167"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Cable, Jennifer"],"country":["Australia","France","Germany","Ireland","Israel","Luxembourg","Spain","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology","Centro Nacional de Investigaciones Cardiovasculares (CNIC)","Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory","Harvard Medical School","Harvard University","Institut Cochin","Johns Hopkins University","Lausanne University Hospital","Luxembourg Institute of Health","Massachusetts General Hospital","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute of Immunobiology and Epigenetics","Monash Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences","National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases","PhD Science Writer","Salk Institute for Biological Studies, Torrey Pines, California, USA.","St Jude Children's Research Hospital","The Ohio State University","The Peter Doherty Institute for Infection and Immunity","Trinity College Dublin","University College Dublin (UCD) School of Medicine","University of California","University of Luxembourg","University of Michigan","University of Michigan Comprehensive Cancer Center","Van Andel Institute","Vanderbilt-Ingram Cancer Center","Weizmann Institute of Science","Yale University"],"keyword":["Cancer","Immunity","Immunometabolism","Immunotherapy","Metabolism","Obesity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunometabolism at the crossroads of obesity and cancer a keystone symposia report","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263853949/nyas.14976.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Sagar P. Bapat was supported by the U.S. National Institutes of Health (NIH) grants F30 DK096828, T32 GM007198, R38 HL143581