Ayo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"høyerpedh","last":"Høyer","name":"Høyer, Klaus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Brogaard","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogaard","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_19","eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831"],"pages":"381-398","place":"Singapore","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160476665"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-68b67171-33fe-4752-badf-5b8f2624cbc9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Communities, Collectives and Categories","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-189140","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Water has the capacity to infrastructure social worlds. From Wittfogel’s (1957) theory of water management and irrigation infrastructures causing the rise of the state as form of governance to Orlove and Caton’s claim – following Mauss - that water is a ‘total social fact’ (Orlove and Caton 2010), water occupies a central place in the social sciences, and increasingly so in times of climatic and environmental changes, when floods, scarcity, and sea level rise, among other challenges affect societies worldwide. Anthropological studies of the meaning of water to culture and society, and of how water and social worlds mutually shape each other, whether in the form of rivers, oceans, aquifers, lakes, or glaciers, anthropological studies of waterworlds are characterised by bringing to the fore material and technological practices as well as political and infrastructural arrangements. This chapter outlines key anthropological studies of water management and distribution, organising these around water flows and the properties of the technologies used to manage and distribute water. An ethnographic case of the ways water infrastructures social and political life in an urban setting in contemporary Peru is presented to discuss how water is simultaneously universal and singular (multiple), and how water infrastructures anthropological theory.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersen, Astrid Oberborbeck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056596"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anthropology","Ethnography","Infrastructure","Materiality","Method","Peru","Technology","Theory","Water"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"water infrastructures the making and maintenance of material and organisational connections","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85160462394&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-056596","identifier":[{"id":"85160482444","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85160462394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-164cc029-fb90-4e9c-a78d-43e98b6a95b0"],"keyword":["Anthropology","Ethnography","Infrastructure","Materiality","Method","Peru","Technology","Theory","Water"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96BF090498F01E672EE5AB6ECC2A4B34"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, The Techno-Anthropology Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Astrid Oberborbeck","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"29717065-a01d-45cb-9f21-a056953ed9bd","name":"Andersen, Astrid Oberborbeck","orcid":"0000-0002-7811-1427","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Brogård","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_37","eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831","9789811670862"],"pages":"721-739","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160462394"],"sdg":["6. Clean Water and Sanitation","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-164cc029-fb90-4e9c-a78d-43e98b6a95b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Water Infrastructures : The Making and Maintenance of Material and Organisational Connections","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056596","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Anthropos and techne are inseparable when it comes to the study of humans and their societies. From its very origins as a discipline, anthropology has recorded and researched human-technology interfaces in efforts to account for and understand forms of social organisation and practice as well as systems of belief and meaning throughout the world. This chapter provides a comprehensive overview of the gradual formation of ‘anthropology of technology’ as a field of enquiry, from early evolutionary studies of technology via critiques of it by those who championed diffusionist understandings, to Maussian approaches to techniques as material actions, technology as skilled practice, and more contemporary understandings of technologies in terms of socio-technical systems and infrastructures. It is exactly such a multiplicity of approaches that has contributed to the thriving anthropologies of technology that make up this field of enquiry, allowing for analytical and methodological scaling on the part of the ethnographer, who can choose to focus on embodied skills, on practices/material actions, or on larger socio-technical systems which, together, make up technologies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bruun, Maja Hojer","Wahlberg, Ayo"],"cuid":["S02-090.22-028052"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the anthropology of technology the formation of a field","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85139557481","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.22-028052","identifier":[{"id":"85139557481","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d4834717-6dfc-4dcc-a44a-5d67e348c24d","ku-3a6cc8da-acc2-43de-85cd-9f05634e9cab"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C544FDDD4F69078576C1CF72971D4E85"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"fd7fa4bb-1d54-43ae-b40c-f5c8acae5f6d","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","orcid":"0000-0002-9877-8800","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"c1114f6e-8a86-4e8b-a7f7-db6ac7b914d5","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","orcid":"0000-0001-6862-5208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication"