{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383242"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"convene represent deliberate reasoning the democratic in embryonic stem cell research oversight committees","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86760565/Douglas_Jones_2022_Convene_Represent_Deliberate.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383242","ids":["itu-86685709-2793-4f7a-aa1c-f80a8d57a86a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A16C54053165848806BD9726407CFFE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86760565/Douglas_Jones_2022_Convene_Represent_Deliberate.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781912729128"],"isbn":["9781912729302"],"pages":"161-186","publisher":"Mattering Press","status":"p","title":"Democratic Situations"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-86685709-2793-4f7a-aa1c-f80a8d57a86a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Convene, Represent, Deliberate? : Reasoning the democratic in embryonic stem cell research oversight committees","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383242","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Understanding how human societies are organised has been at the very core of anthropology since its inception as a scientific discipline in the nineteenth century. While early twentieth-century social anthropologists set out to characterise the kinship, economic, and political systems that shaped the social life of ‘communal’ societies, by the end of the century, a new style of ethnography had emerged. This chapter provides a genealogy of ‘assemblage ethnography’, showing how it developed as a methodological response to the challenge of understanding social organisation across scales, sites, and practices in a ‘hypercomplex’ technologising and globalising world through three iterations: (1) governmentality-inspired ethnographies that take dispositifs as their object; (2) multi-sited ethnographic studies of how biomedicine is being harnessed to administer and enhance ‘life itself’; and (3) approaches that have deployed a more fluid understanding of assemblages to capture the rhizome-like ways that macro, meso, and micro scales are connected. Assemblage ethnography has become a key approach within anthropology generally, and the anthropology of technology specifically, because of its ability to locate sited ethnographies within the broader complexes that are characteristic of a world in which daily lives are constantly (re-)shaped by technoscience, laws, regulations, technocracies, institutions, and forms of expertise.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wahlberg, Ayo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-484287"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assemblage ethnography configurations across scales sites and practices","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/361699501/Wahlberg.2022.AssemblageEthnographyConfigurations.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-484287","identifier":[{"id":"85160488918","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-980283c3-f963-4ffb-a64f-7a148ae96cee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A583BA4FE21F4841CF9AA2E963FA893F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/361699501/Wahlberg.2022.AssemblageEthnographyConfigurations.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"c1114f6e-8a86-4e8b-a7f7-db6ac7b914d5","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","orcid":"0000-0001-6862-5208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Brogård","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_6","eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831"],"pages":"125-144","place":"Singapore","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160488918"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-980283c3-f963-4ffb-a64f-7a148ae96cee"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Assemblage Ethnography : Configurations Across Scales, Sites, and Practices","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-484287","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The desire to become better is at heart of human existence. This claim has been advocated, criticised, contested, and explored philosophically and empirically in studies of enhancement and optimisation-terms that refer to practices oriented towards betterment of the self and interventions in the present to create a better future. Today the terms optimisation and enhancement are not only associated with specialised disciplines but also with everyday practices where they reflect a moral imperative for human being to always strive to become better versions of themselves. The purpose of this chapter is twofold: firstly, to present the two terms and map the different positions in the discussion, mainly based on the work of scholars within bioethics; secondly, drawing from anthropological and qualitative work on pharmaceutical enhancement and self-tracking, the chapter will show how anthropological and qualitative studies have nuanced the bioethical debate as well as given rise to new sets of questions. Ultimately it is argued that both these practices inscribe themselves into societal values to produce a response to them.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kristensen, Dorthe Brogaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-595796"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bioethics","Enhancement","Optimisation","Pharmaceutical","Self tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the optimised and enhanced self experiences of the self and the making of societal values","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85141239093","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-595796","identifier":[{"id":"85141239093","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4ed16cfd-c1fd-447a-b747-177f74b62cc0"],"keyword":["Bioethics","Enhancement","Optimisation","Pharmaceutical","Self-tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1EE16A96471CF44FCAF6889F0DF5991"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Brogaard","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a9b43877-9747-46c6-ae54-fa91cad9a1f6","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogaard","orcid":"0000-0002-9008-9349","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"høyerpedh","last":"Høyer","name":"Høyer, Klaus","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Brogård","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","n