{"author_count":14,"contributors":["Bruun, Maja Hojer","Wahlberg, Ayo","Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Hasse, Cathrine","Hoeyer, Klaus","Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739232"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preface","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739232","identifier":[{"id":"85160464265","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-657bee4a-d29a-4668-ac47-4a854d3a1aed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-62A21B225B01106D3E583A0384A9747A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"c1114f6e-8a86-4e8b-a7f7-db6ac7b914d5","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","orcid":"0000-0001-6862-5208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepau","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpau","last":"Hoeyer","locid":"155a3763-e58a-4576-8cd9-5042f6a9947f","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0002-2780-4784","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Dorthe Brogård","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Drothe Brogård","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Drothe Brogård","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831"],"place":"Singapore","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-657bee4a-d29a-4668-ac47-4a854d3a1aed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preface","type":"Book Preface, Encycl. Entry","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739232","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Most technologies are knowledge-intensive, and contemporary knowledge production is often technology-intensive. Hence, knowledge practices are a central theme for a handbook for the anthropology of technology. Knowledge about knowing has mostly been considered a branch of philosophy or alternatively of theology. In this section we argue that the study of knowledge practices is part of both the foundation of the anthropological discipline and its future as we attend to technology-mediated forms of knowing, unknowing, and re-knowing. The section highlights the variations and multiplicities of knowing. It shows that studying knowledge and forms of knowing implies exploring forms of unknowing and ignorance. The seven contributions to this section present research on processes through which knowledge is made, what becomes silenced in the process, and how anthropology often holds a special role in bringing such lost insights or alternative forms of knowing back into the light. Each of the chapters presents a unique take on human engagement with knowledge and technologies of knowing, thereby continuing a long tradition of studying the production of knowledge as socially embedded and materially ingrained.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hoeyer, Klaus","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S02-084.06-038280"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Anthropology of Technology","Forms of Unknowing","Knowledge practices","Socially Embedded Knowledge","Technology Mediated Knowing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"knowing unknowing and reknowing","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_11","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.06-038280","identifier":[{"id":"85160464996","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-325bd014-72d9-4b5d-86b6-0cfe93f38f63","ku-756b9edf-9f42-4f2e-bd0c-5f04b2bb2fa0"],"keyword":["Anthropology of Technology","Forms of Unknowing","Knowledge Practices","Socially Embedded Knowledge","Technology-Mediated Knowing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DE6F4A22121A7E2710CB5C5C6F4E7C06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://static-curis.ku.dk/portal/files/301105380/Hoeyer_Winthereik_KnowingUnknowingAndRe_knowing._anthropology_of_technology_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/301105380/Hoeyer_Winthereik_KnowingUnknowingAndRe_knowing._anthropology_of_technology_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_11","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpau","last":"Hoeyer","locid":"155a3763-e58a-4576-8cd9-5042f6a9947f","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0002-2780-4784","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe B","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe B","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_11","edition":"1","isbn":["9789811670831"],"pages":"217-235","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160464996"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-325bd014-72d9-4b5d-86b6-0cfe93f38f63","ku-756b9edf-9f42-4f2e-bd0c-5f04b2bb2fa0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Knowing, Unknowing, and Reknowing","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.06-038280","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This section presents infrastructures as a matter of anthropological concern and argues that attention to infrastructuring—that is, the processes through which infrastructures shape and are shaped by social, cultural, and political life—is a key element for the anthropology of technology. The inherent relationality of infrastructures and infrastructuring, this section shows, is an occasion for anthropologists to attend to infrastructures as both ‘product’ and process without necessarily having to do a study of ‘an infrastructure’. In contemporary social life, thinking in terms of infrastructuring is exactly what allows ethnographers to study, for example, global interconnectedness across multiple scales, sites, and practices, including digitalisation practices and politics, the climate crisis, pandemic governance, multinational corporations, financial systems, deforestation, biodiversity, welfare, and much more that happens on a more-than-human scale. By paying close attention to the methods and effects of infrastructuring, anthropologists will be better equipped to analyse the role of infrastructure in social life and politics.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Winthereik, Brit Ross","Wahlberg, Ayo"],"cuid":["S02-085.88-038378"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["FLOW","Material instalment","Politics","Process","Relationality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructures linkages and livelihoods","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85160504930","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-085.88-038378","identifier":[{"id":"85160504930","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c2808598-6630-477a-aa87-ff87e6575c8f","ku-70ede242-ece0-4c79-b912-841e07c8f334"],"keyword":["Material instalment","Politics","Relationality","flow","process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A86662B2146A7F855773AB761B4A61E3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"c1114f6e-8a86-4e8b-a7f7-db6ac7b914d5","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","orcid":"0000-0001-6862-5208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hojer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hojer","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Brogård","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorthe Brogård","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_34","eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831"],"pages":"673-687","place":"Singapore","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160504930"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c2808598-6630-477a-aa87-ff87e6575c8f","ku-70ede242-ece0-4c79-b912-841e07c8f334"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructures, Linkages, and Livelihoods","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.88-038378","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is heritable and a potential consequence of exposure to traumatic stress. Evidence suggests that a quantitative approach to PTSD phenotype measurement and incorporation of lifetime trauma exposure (LTE) information could enhance the discovery power of PTSD genome-wide association studies (GWASs). Methods: A GWAS on PTSD symptoms was performed in 51 cohorts followed by a fixed-effects meta-analysis (N = 182,199 European ancestry participants). A GWAS of LTE burden was performed in the UK Biobank cohort (N = 132,988). Genetic correlations were evaluated with linkage disequilibrium score regression. Multivariate analysis was performed using Multi-Trait Analysis of GWAS. Functional mapping and annotation of leading loci was performed with FUMA. Replication was evaluated using the Million Veteran Program GWAS of PTSD total symptoms. Results: GWASs of PTSD symptoms and LTE burden identified 5 and 6 independent genome-wide significant loci, respectively. There was a 72% genetic correlation between PTSD and LTE. PTSD and LTE showed largely similar patterns of genetic correlation with other traits, albeit with some distinctions. Adjusting PTSD for LTE reduced PTSD heritability by 31%. Multivariate analysis of PTSD and LTE increased the effective sample size of the PTSD GWAS by 20% and identified 4 additional loci. Four of these 9 PTSD loci were independently replicated in the Million Veteran Program. Conclusions: Through using a quantitative trait measure of PTSD, we identified novel risk loci not previously identified using prior case-control analyses. PTSD and LTE have a high genetic overlap that can be leveraged to increase discovery power through multivariate methods.","author_count":196,"contributors":["Maihofer, Adam X.","Choi, Karmel W.","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Daskalakis, Nikolaos P.","Denckla, Christy A.","Ketema, Elizabeth","Morey, Rajendra A.","Polimanti, Renato","Ratanatharathorn, Andrew","Torres, Ka