{"abstract":"Reflecting on a methodological experiment, we discuss the use of computational techniques in anthropology. The experiment was based on a collaborative effort by a team of ethnographers to produce an archive on the digitalisation of everyday life that took place during the COVID-19 pandemic. We describe how online ethnographic data collection took place using digitally mediated interviews, participant observation in virtual events, and mobile ethnography. We analyse the consequences of online ethnography for establishing rapport and present steps taken to create an infrastructure for navigating ethnographic material comprising more than 3000 pages of text generated by multiple ethnographers.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Munk, Anders Kristian","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S02-091.55-004565"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Collaboration","Computational anthropology","Computational ethnography","Corona crisis","Covid 19","Digital Methods","Digital anthropology","Digital ethnography","Digitalization","Everyday life","Experiment in infrastructure","Methods","Online ethnography"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational ethnography a case of covid 000000000019 s methodological consequences","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_10","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.55-004565","identifier":[{"id":"85150526456","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5e27d3dd-35a7-470d-9e3a-e90bb558733f","itu-84d0d095-c69f-49d4-a5c6-6113f785dd73"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Collaboration","Computational anthropology","Computational ethnography","Corona crisis","Digital Methods","Digital anthropology","Digitalization","Everyday Life","Experiment in infrastructure","Online ethnography","digital ethnography","methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-338BCFE6ACAD1B54DD0CBA9B2DFB31FD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, The Techno-Anthropology Lab","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Kristian","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","locid":"1152f3e1-f7da-4ced-8a78-b16a32675dca","name":"Munk, Anders Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-5542-3065","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja","key":"hojerbruunpedh","last":"Hojer Bruun","name":"Hojer Bruun, Maja","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja Hoejer","key":"bruunpedh","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Maja Hoejer","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpedh","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespedh","last":"Douglas-Jones","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"hassepedh","last":"Hasse","name":"Hasse, Cathrine","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"hoeyerpedh","last":"Hoeyer","name":"Hoeyer, Klaus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe","key":"brogårdkristensenpedh","last":"Brogård Kristensen","name":"Brogård Kristensen, Dorthe","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorte Brogaard","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Dorte Brogaard","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit","key":"rosswinthereikpedh","last":"Ross Winthereik","name":"Ross Winthereik, Brit","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpedh","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-16-7084-8_10","eisbn":["9789811670848"],"isbn":["9789811670831"],"pages":"201-214","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave Handbook of the Anthropology of Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150526456"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5e27d3dd-35a7-470d-9e3a-e90bb558733f","itu-84d0d095-c69f-49d4-a5c6-6113f785dd73"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computational Ethnography: A Case of COVID-19’s Methodological Consequences","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.55-004565","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Anthropology is founded on the notion of the human as a mortal and moral being. Based on a literature review, we show that anthropological scholarship on morality in the life sciences disturbs this notion of the human; rather, we direct analytical attention to the edges of the human and to the moral and mortal human as connected and vulnerable to other humans, animals, and environments. We then unfold these insights through empirical studies from a research laboratory using piglets as animal models and a clinical genetics department diagnosing children with rare diseases. Although the use of nonhuman animals in biomedical research appears morally unproblematic, the daily care for suffering piglets turns them into near humans. Human genomes, on the other hand, are closely tied to the person, yet in research and clinical practices, genomes are constantly moved out of the category of the person. This analysis compels us not simply to accept the human as the founding category of anthropology, but turn it into an empirical enquiry. Studying how the human is enacted in the life sciences promises both to grasp and exceed the conditions of possibility for the study of morality and value in technological practices.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Svendsen, Mette Nordahl","Dam, Mie Seest","Navne, Laura Emdal","Gjødsbøl, Iben Mundbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-092.57-044497"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biopolitics","Etik Antropologi Etnografi Kvalitativ metode","Kinship","Life science","Morality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"OT":["Institut for Folkesundhedsvidenskab"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"moral ambiguities fleshy and digital substitutes in the life sciences","src":["ku","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85160466221","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.57-044497","identifier":[{"id":"85160466221","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-944dee60-0158-4d9f-a4df-006f39f19d4a","vive-290bf3db-19dd-4676-80c5-1e5099252ddc"],"keyword":["Etik, Antropologi, Etnografi, Kvalitativ metode","biopolitics","kinship","life science","morality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-99E3146EEFF3D8BB8EE5CF0AEDC6303C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut for Folkesundhedsvidenskab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mette Nordahl","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"2ef090a5-f103-467c-9bf5-207c0858cc08","name":"Svendsen, Mette Nordahl","orcid":"0000-00