":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Mattering Press","status":"p","title":"Sensing In/Security"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b00d8c29-9ae7-455e-9434-7e23ce55b1f9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Visual Vignettes","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383831","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Ballestero’s book is about how the work of valuing water is done, away from the glossy images, hashtags and videos of a single day campaign. An early decision, Ballestero tells us, was that her ‘ethnographic account was going to focus on the dimensions of water that would never make it into National Geographic pictures’, nor would she entertain the call of ‘watery mystique’ (187). Instead, A Future History of Water charts the ‘enormous amount of “deskwork” (186) that goes into working with the ‘fairly unexciting matter of the technical concepts that organize water’s availability’ (187). While its largest framing is the way the categories “right” and “commodity” manage (and are managed in) the making of water futures, the work that fascinates her – to which she brings her ethnographically attuned wonder – is seemingly mundane, taking place in the ‘back corners of bureaucratic offices and in Kafkaesque congressional procedures’ (195). In those corners, offices, and meeting rooms, she sits, listens and talks with activists, experts and public officials as they tweak, adapt and change their tools for engaging the vast issues of what it means to pay for, care for, and manage water in the now.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383929"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Water"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a future history of water rachel douglas jones comments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://allegralaboratory.net/a-future-history-of-water-rachel-douglas-jones-comments/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383929","ids":["itu-b67f8b25-9ce2-47b7-a5f7-5975926be07c"],"keyword":["water"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-33C5B942620686CABE5F1C54A5A9DB56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://allegralaboratory.net/a-future-history-of-water-rachel-douglas-jones-comments/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-b67f8b25-9ce2-47b7-a5f7-5975926be07c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"#A future history of water: Rachel Douglas-Jones’ comments","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383929","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The world is talking ‘data’. The early cross‐disciplinary, business‐orientated hype around the potential of ‘big’ data, with its promises of unprecedented insight into social life, has given way. Data now motivates a sweep of dystopian visions, from rampant commodification to the invasion of privacy, political manipulation, and shadowy data doubles. Yet anthropologists have been cautious in taking data itself as their object, even as the social life of data practices becomes manifest in our ethnographies. In this introduction, we argue for an anthropology of data that is ethnographically specific and theoretically ambitious, putting forward a case for why anthropological engagements with the data moment might be not only politically important but also conceptually generative.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Walford, Antonia","Seaver, Nick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381253"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tufts University","University College London"],"keyword":["Big data","Data anthropology","Data practices","Ethnographic methods","Political implications of data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction towards an anthropology of data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86037625/0._JRAI_May_2020_Introduction.docx","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381253","identifier":[{"id":"85102455639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0064c3c1-b2cc-44c7-bca3-fdd84be66b64"],"keyword":["Big data","Data anthropology","Data practices","Ethnographic methods","Political implications of data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-68AAAAFE87678EF0C410BDDB39277784"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86037625/0._JRAI_May_2020_Introduction.docx","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"tufts university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Tufts University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonia","key":"walfordpau","last":"Walford","name":"Walford, Antonia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nick","key":"seaverpau","last":"Seaver","name":"Seaver, Nick","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1467-9655.13477","issn":["13590987","14679655"],"issn_org":["13590987"],"issue":"s1","journal":"Journal of the Royal Anthropological Institute","pages":"9-25","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Royal Anthropological Institute","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID