{"abstract":"How does STS ethnography meet what it researches? Not prescriptive methodology – we were interested in methodography, describing and problematising how methods shape data. 2018 saw three research events that focused on data infrastructures and practices in participant observation and in collaborating with other actants in & around the field. With this focus, we turned back and looked at our own research practices. This meant exploring what kind of performative relations arise between STS and our topics of research and how these relations were materially and otherwise shaped.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lippert, Ingmar","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382753"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data","Method","Science and Technology Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"doing data methodography in and of sts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://easst.net/article/doing-data-methodography-in-and-of-sts/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382753","ids":["itu-62e4cd29-8e84-492a-876d-11dc2dda3d10"],"keyword":["Science and Technology Studies","data","method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CB3B80D24EB2B6CA1A6CCABA0B14215B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://easst.net/article/doing-data-methodography-in-and-of-sts/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingmar","key":"lippertpau","last":"Lippert","name":"Lippert, Ingmar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13845160"],"issue":"1","journal":"EASST Review","pages":"35-39","status":"p","title":"EASST Review","title_org":"EASST Review (European Association for the Study of Science and Technology)","volume":"38"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-62e4cd29-8e84-492a-876d-11dc2dda3d10"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Doing Data” : Methodography in and of STS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382753","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This article is concerned with strategies to bolster ethical review against insinuations that it might not be well done. My discussion traces doubts about the competences of ethics review committees in low and middle income settings to ask how a real ethical review is known, and for whom it must be evidenced. Drawing on ethnographic fieldwork amongst committees participating in the Forum of Ethics Review Committees of Asia and the Western Pacific, an organization started in 2000 to support grass-roots regional networking and capacity building, I describe three mechanisms by which a ‘real’ review can be identified, and pre-emptively distinguished from a ‘pseudo’ review. I argue that each strategy is premised on articulating a different facet of ethical interiority. By contextualizing ethical review within histories of debates about global health research ethics, and a growth in regional responses to build local capacity, I explore how geographies of competence motivate responses to anxieties about whether and how ethical review can be made real.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382076"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Accreditation","Asia Paciﬁc","Committees","Doubt","Integrity","ethics review"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"getting inside ethical review anxious bureaucracies of revelation anticipation and virtue","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84704313/Getting_Inside_Ethical_Review_Final_OA_Compliant_SherpaRomeo.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382076","identifier":[{"id":"85067248102","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36c717a2-393e-4de3-bc42-c26f101a29f5"],"keyword":["Accreditation","Asia-Paciﬁc","committees","doubt","ethics review","integrity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E80728F6CD843FD1B94F6D65FBE404F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84704313/Getting_Inside_Ethical_Review_Final_OA_Compliant_SherpaRomeo.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09581596.2019.1591615","issn":["09581596","14693682"],"issn_org":["09581596"],"issue":"4","journal":"Critical Public Health","pages":"448-459","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Critical Public Health","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067248102"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36c717a2-393e-4de3-bc42-c26f101a29f5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Getting inside ethical review: anxious bureaucracies of revelation, anticipation and virtue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382076","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Subcortical brain structures are integral to motion, consciousness, emotions and learning. We identified common genetic variation related to the volumes of the nucleus accumbens, amygdala, brainstem, caudate nucleus, globus pallidus, putamen and thalamus, using genome-wide association analyses in almost 40,000 individuals from CHARGE, ENIGMA and UK Biobank. We show that variability in subcortical volumes is heritable, and identify 48 significantly associated loci (40 novel at the time of analysis). Annotation of these loci by utilizing gene expression, methylation and neuropathological data identified 199 genes putatively implicated in neurodevelopment, synaptic signaling, axonal transport, apoptosis, inflammation/infection and susceptibility to neurological disorders. This set of genes is significantly enriched for Drosophila orthologs associated with neurodevelopmental phenotypes, suggesting evolutionarily conserved mechanisms. Our findings uncover novel biology and potential drug targets underlying brain development and disease.","author_count":289,"contributors":["Satizabal, Claudia L.","Adams, Hieab H.H.","Hibar, Derrek P.","White, Charles C.","Knol, Maria J.","Stein, Jason L.","Scholz, Markus","Sargurupremraj, Muralidharan","Jahanshad, Neda","Roshchupkin, Gennady V.","Smith, Albert V.","Bis, Joshua C.","Jian, Xueqiu","Luciano, Michelle","Hofer, Edith","Teumer, Alexander","van der Lee, Sven J.","Yang, Jingyun","Yanek, Lisa R.","Lee, Tom V.","Li, Shuo","Hu, Yanhui","Koh, Jia Yu","Eicher, John D.","Desrivières, Sylvane","Arias-Vasquez, Alejandro","Chauhan, Ganesh","Athanasiu, Lavinia","Rentería, Miguel E.","Kim, Sungeun","Hoehn, David","Armstrong, Nicola J.","Chen, Qiang","Holmes, Avram J.","den Braber, Anouk","Kloszewska, Iwona","Andersson, Micael","Espeseth, Thomas","Grimm, Oliver","Abramovic, Lucija","Alhusaini, Saud","Milaneschi, Yuri","Papmeyer, Martina","Axelsson, Tomas","Ehrlich, Stefan","Roiz-Santiañez, Roberto","Kraemer, Bernd","Håberg, Asta