{"abstract":"Capacity building is a pervasive idea that has received little critical treatment from anthropology. In this introduction, we outline the growing use of the idea of ‘capacity building’ within and beyond development settings, and highlight mechanisms by which it gains footholds in both policy and practice. is special issue centres and questions its histories, assumptions, intentions and enactments in order to bring ethnographic attention to the promises it entails. By bringing together cases from di erent sectors and continents, the collection pursues capacity building’s self-evident character, opening up what capacities themselves are thought to be. By not taking capacity building’s promises for granted, the articles collected here have two aims: to interrogate the means of capacity building’s ubiquity, and to develop critical purchase on its persuasive power.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Shaffner, Justin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383755"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The New Centre for Research and Practice"],"keyword":["Capacity","Comparison","Development","Hope","Improvement","Insufficiency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction capacity building in ethnographic comparison","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/cja.2017.350102","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383755","ids":["itu-ab4ece3b-7d5d-4055-ab2a-b158353d8df4"],"keyword":["capacity","comparison","development","hope","improvement","insufficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-81AEC35C9571A7CB5AFDA8DEB44B2A48"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82111241/0._Douglas_Jones_Shaffner_Introduction.docx","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/cja.2017.350102","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"the new centre for research and practice","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The New Centre for Research and Practice","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin","key":"shaffnerpau","last":"Shaffner","name":"Shaffner, Justin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3167/cja.2017.350102","issn":["03057674","20477716"],"issn_org":["03057674"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Cambridge Journal of Anthropology","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Berghahn Books","status":"p","title":"The Cambridge Journal of Anthropology","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ab4ece3b-7d5d-4055-ab2a-b158353d8df4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction: Capacity Building in Ethnographic Comparison","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383755","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Simpson, Bob","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384674"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anthropology","Death","Donation","Values"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new immortalities death donation and dedication in the twenty first century","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17157/mat.4.4.308","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384674","ids":["itu-e74be8c1-fa1b-475d-bcd9-ddc4d1240d92"],"keyword":["anthropology","death","donation","values"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AC2687B156278760542B5F55E586F36C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17157/mat.4.4.308","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025809/New_Immortalities_2017_postprint.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83126646/sp_simpson_mat_v4_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bob","key":"simpsonpau","last":"Simpson","name":"Simpson, Bob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17157/mat.4.4.308","issn":["2405691X"],"issue":"4","journal":"MAT Medicine Anthropology Theory","pages":"1-21","publisher":"University of Amsterdam","status":"p","title":"MAT Medicine Anthropology Theory","title_org":"Medicine Anthropology Theory","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e74be8c1-fa1b-475d-bcd9-ddc4d1240d92"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"New Immortalities : Death, donation and dedication in the twenty-first century","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384674","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The historic environment undergoes cycles of material deterioration, and these processes have a powerful impact on the meanings and values associated with it. In particular, decay informs the experience of authenticity, as a tangible mark of age and ‘the real’. This article examines the intersection between material transformation, scientific intervention and cultural value. Drawing on qualitative social research at three Scottish historic buildings, we show that there are a complex range of cultural values and qualities associated with material transformation. Furthermore, we highlight how the use of science-based conservation to characterise, and intervene in, processes of material transformation can affect these values and qualities. We argue that it is necessary and important to consider the cultural ramifications of such interventions alongside their material effects. This requires a case-by-case approach, because the cultural values and qualities associated with material transformation are context-specific and vary with different kinds of monuments and materials. We conclude with a series of recommendations aimed at integrating humanities and science-based approaches to transformation in the historic environment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Hughes, John","Jones, Sian","Yarrow, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383447"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Decay","Qualitative Research","Science","Technology","Value","auth"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"science value and material decay in the conservation of historic environments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","ur